/-!
# Explicit colorings for candidate Frattini quotients

These are finite binary groups and color tables, not asserted models of
the concrete J₄ candidates. The separate realization contract requires
a genuine quotient isomorphism and invariance under candidate automorphisms.
The stabilizer bounds are also separate proof obligations.

The table indices match `Candidates.Data`. Colors were computed from
order-centralizer fiber profiles; the source JSON retains the quotient
basis words, proposed Frattini words, counts, and original GAP rows.
Neither these calculations nor the reported ranks are Lean certificates.
Source context: Aschbacher–Smith 1.3.4, printed p.511/PDF p.528.
-/

